    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "For Sale by Public Auction will take place at 3pm on Thursday, 22nd October 2026, at The Listowel Arms Hotel, The Square, Listowel, Co. Kerry – In one or more lots.\r\n\r\nAn exceptional opportunity awaits near Listowel with this approx. 46.3 Acre residential holding, featuring an elevated setting with panoramic countryside views.  Located just 9km from both Listowel town and Ballylongford village, the property is accessed via a 0.7km shared private cul-de-sac laneway and offers massive potential for farmers, investors, or those seeking a rewarding restoration project.  The holding includes a detached 4-bedroom farmhouse - vacant for over two years and highly eligible for vacant home refurbishment grants - alongside an extensive farmyard equipped with a modern cattle shed, slurry storage, and versatile outbuildings.  Divided by the shared private lane (right of way) into two convenient parcels, the land is generally of good quality and currently utilized for silage production, though parts would benefit from drainage and re-seeding.\r\n\r\nTo accommodate all buyers, the property will be offered for sale by public auction in three flexible lots:\r\n\r\nLot 1:  Folio KY36377F – Plan 101 & Part of Folio KY6957 – Plan 14.  The residential hub, comprising the 4-bedroom dwelling, the extensive farmyard, and approx. 26.39 acres of land in one parcel (serviced by an on-site well, septic tank, and electricity).  Guide Price - €330,000.\r\n\r\nLot 2:  Part of Folio KY6957 – Plan 14.  A non-residential parcel comprising approx. 19.9 acres of quality land with no buildings or services..  Guide Price - €169,000.\r\n\r\nLot 3:  Folio KY36377F – Plan 101 & Folio KY6957 – Plan 14.  The entire 46.3-acre holding.  Guide Price - €499,000.\r\n\r\nThe public auction will take place at 3pm on Thursday, 22nd October 2026, at The Listowel Arms Hotel, The Square, Listowel, Co. Kerry.  \r\n\r\nViewing is highly advised to fully appreciate the sheer potential and scenic beauty of this North Kerry gem.\r\n\r\nSolicitors with carriage of sale:  Ms Margarita Purtill. Purtill Woulfe Murphy Solicitors, Upper Church Street, Listowel, Co. Kerry. Tel 068 28766"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Rooms",
        "SortOrder": 2,
        "Content": "Front Entrance Porch - 3.9m x 5.2m \r\nLeading into living/dining room with vinyl flooring, Stanley No. 9 solid fuel range and staircase to first floor.\r\n\r\nSitting Room - 5.0m x 3.6m \r\nWith fitted carpet - dual aspect. \r\n\r\nBedroom 1 - 3.6m x 2.7m \r\nWith fitted carpet.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 - 3.6m x 2.3m \r\n\r\n\r\nKitchen - 2.5m x 2.3m \r\nPlumbed for washing machine, fitted sink and tiled splash back.\r\n\r\nBathroom - 3.4m x 1.8m \r\nWith bath, shower, toilet and washing basin.\r\n\r\nRear Entrance Lobby - 1.2m x 2.2m \r\nWith access door to rear yard.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor Landing - 1.5m x 1.3m \r\nWith toilet and wash basin.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 (Attic Room) - 2.6m x 3.2m \r\nWith gable window and latted ceiling.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4 & Store Room - 7.9m x 3.5m \r\nRestricted head height, Velux roof light and gable window.\r\n\r\nOutside Accommodation - \r\n\r\n\r\nCow Stalls 29m x 5m - 29.0m x 5.0m \r\nTraditional style cow stalls, store and garage of masonry construction with pitched galvanised roof and lean-to roof with charming original features, including cobble floor.\r\n\r\nHaybarn 21.5m x 14m - 21.5m x 14.0m \r\nLarge 3 bay round roof haybarn with lean-to sheds on either side.  One lean-to is set out as a cow stall/milking area, the remaining space is used for hay/straw storage and machinery.\r\n\r\nAdjoining Dairy - 3.7m x 3.7m \r\nWith refrigerated tank and association equipment.\r\n\r\nLarge Concrete Yard - \r\nLarge concrete yard and underground water storage tank.\r\n\r\nCubicle House - \r\nPurpose built cubicle house of steel and concrete construction with pitched cement fibre roof, 2 x electric scrapers and easy feed barrier with external slatted tank, agitating points and underground slurry storage tank.\r\n\r\nEnclosed Gated Yard - \r\nEnclosed gated yard with cattle handling facility.\r\n\r\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Peaceful setting on an elevated site commanding views of the surrounding countryside\r\nDouble glazed PVC windows and doors. \r\nDual heating system - external oil heat pack and solid fuel range.\r\nPrivate well supply and on-site septic tank.\r\nBlock built house with insulated slab board on inner leaf of external walls.\r\nPebble dash exterior and pitched slate roof.\r\nRight of way through subject holding in favour of neighbouring property."
      },
